<BaseLayout title="About" description="How Physics Ledger publishes stable mathematical-physics notes." canonicalPath="/about/">
  <article class="page-intro shell prose"><p class="section-label">About</p><h1>How the notebook works</h1><p>Each entry is a permanent Markdown page with validated TeX, a stable ID, and source links. Discussion remains separate in GitHub.</p><h2>Publishing</h2><ol><li>Generate a complete Markdown entry in chat.</li><li>Assign an unused immutable ID.</li><li>Save, validate, commit, and push.</li></ol><h2>Mathematics</h2><p>TeX is validated and rendered to SVG during the build. Original TeX remains available to copy and to machine-readable endpoints. Full TeX packages such as TikZ are intentionally outside the first release.</p><h2>Discussion privacy</h2><p>Optional comments use public GitHub Discussions and require GitHub sign-in. They are not the canonical learning record.</p></article>
</BaseLayout>
